cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "eu-lng-network-governance: Python scripts for EU LNG Network Analysis"
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.19924877"
date-released: "2026-04-30"
authors:
  - family-names: "Roy"
    given-names: "Jeremy"
license: "MIT License"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChanceScientist/eu-lng-network-governance"
abstract: >
  This release provides the complete reproducible workflow for constructing,
  normalizing, and analyzing the EU LNG trade network (2015–2025). The pipeline
  includes temporal network construction, normalization of directed weighted
  graphs, structural and flow-based metrics, Louvain community detection,
  adjacent-period community matching, transition matrices, stability indices,
  structural signatures, governance indicators, and visualization scripts.
  Raw UN Comtrade data are not bundled with this release due to licensing
  restrictions; users must download the relevant monthly trade flow files
  (HS 271111, EU-27 reporters) directly from the UN Comtrade Database and place
  them in the data_raw/ directory.
message: >
  If you use this work, please cite this release using the
  metadata provided here or the DOI assigned via Zenodo.
